+# Real local document workflow
+
+These scripts use the actual Flutter web build, React UI, ASP.NET API, FastAPI and a dedicated PostgreSQL cluster. They do not intercept application API responses. Run from repository root, in order: integrated_workflow.cjs, resume_workflow.cjs, complete_review.cjs. The implementation copies used for the recorded execution remain in qmse-output/completion-20261008/audit.
+
+Prerequisites: local services on 55443 API, 55444 FastAPI, 55446 PostgreSQL, 55447 React, 55448 Flutter; database qmse_workflow, synthetic seeded clerk/admin; /private/tmp/qmse-completion-control/settings.json with locally generated password and AI bridge key, and a writable private control directory. The recorded service supervisor and setup logs are in the evidence package. Never substitute a production connection. Build Flutter web and configure its generated asset .env for the local API before serving it. Keep private browser storage and tokens outside the repository.
+
+The first script creates a fresh synthetic customer/request and private browser state. The second uploads a genuine bundled PDF through Flutter and two genuine sample PDFs through the API, gets real deterministic FastAPI clerk recommendations, and performs explicit admin assignment. The third executes React human review, verifies Flutter synchronization and queries PostgreSQL. Consult integrated-result.json and HTTP/database evidence for success; intermediate scripts can save blocked attempts without a nonzero exit code. Complete Golden Case model acceptance and native-device testing are separate.
